    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by the elite 80+ scores of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Yordan Alvarez** (80.21). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play; while he faces Michael Lorenzen, the confluence of a favorable 4.35 xERA, a wind-out advantage, and a 14% boost from a dynamic platoon edge makes him our most efficient source of stolen bases. Simultaneously, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in must-start despite facing a right-handed arm; his elite xwOBA of 0.453 and a significant 15% boost from facing a mid-tier starter solidify his status as the cornerstone of our lineup. **Junior Caminero** also projects extremely well (70.04) against Eric Lauer, benefiting from a soft 4.63 xERA and a generous 15% SP skill adjustment.\n\nNavigating the remainder of the lineup, **Trea Turner** (63.89) is a vital asset, specifically because Ryan Gusto\u2019s slow delivery profile provides a 4% efficiency bump for **Trea Turner** to capitalize on the basepaths\u2014a critical factor in our focus on the scarce SB category. **Kyle Schwarber** (60.51) rounds out our top-tier starts, leveraging a lead-off spot to maximize his plate appearances. The closest bench decision today involved **Nelson Velazquez** (47.91) and **Dillon Dingler** (42.24); while **Nelson Velazquez** maintains a superior 0.440 xwOBA, the scarcity of the catcher position and the need for structural balance across the lineup ultimately kept **Dillon Dingler** in the primary slot. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given that all lineups are currently pending; we are projecting based on historical order, but any shift for **Carson Benge** (48.31) or **Dillon Dingler** could see their efficiency scores fluctuate. We are closely monitoring the status of **Christian Yelich** and **Caleb Durbin**, both of whom are unavailable today due to team off-days, and we continue to track **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds** as they remain stashed in the minors. The Zebras are well-positioned, provided our core hitters capitalize on the favorable xERA matchups against the likes of Troy Melton and Michael Lorenzen.",
